.TH UPC\-TTY\-BRIDGE 1 "2026-10-30" "unheaded 49690433" "Unheaded Kingdom"
.SH NAME
upc\-tty\-bridge \- Bridge UPC TTY byte streams to browser terminals over WebSocket (ASCEND\-LINUX Mode A).
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B upc\-tty\-bridge
[\fIOPTION\fR]...
.SH DESCRIPTION
Bridge UPC TTY byte streams to browser terminals over WebSocket (ASCEND\-LINUX Mode A).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-listen \fISTRING\fR
listen address (host:port); loopback by default (default 127.0.0.1:26100)
.TP
.B \-\-listen\-unix \fIPATH\fR
also serve ingest and drain on this unix socket PATH (mode 0660), for upc\-bootctl inside a netns; off when empty
.TP
.B \-\-port \fIN\fR
deprecated: listen on 127.0.0.1:<port> (use \-\-listen)
.TP
.B \-\-pprof \fIADDR\fR
serve net/http/pprof on this loopback ADDR (e.g. 127.0.0.1:6060); off when empty
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
display this help and exit
.TP
.B \-V, \-\-version
output version information and exit
.SH EXAMPLES
.EX
upc\-tty\-bridge \-\-port 26100
upc\-tty\-bridge \-\-listen\-unix /run/unheaded/upc\-tty.sock   then UPC_TTY_BRIDGE_SOCKET=/run/unheaded/upc\-tty.sock for upc\-bootctl
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR unheaded (1)
